OSI (Open systems interconnection) model - Provides a framework dicatating how all networked devices will send, receive and interpret data.
  OSI model layers (7):
    Layer 1 (Physical) - Simply, this layer references the physical components of the hardware used in networking. Devices use binary 0 and 1.
    Layer 2 (Data link) - Focuses on the physical addressing of the transmission. Receives a packet from the netowrk layer and adds in the physical MAC address of the receiving endpoint.
    Layer 3 (Network) - Routing and re-assembly of data takes place. In this layer everything is dealt with via IP adresses.
    Layer 4 (Transport) - Plays a vital part in transmitting data across a network. Data sent between devices follow TCP and UDP.
