NIC (Network interface card) - Comes with a unique MAC address to identify it.
Encapsulation - Pieces of information get added to data.
OSFP (Open shortest first path) - Calculates the most efficient path to each destination.
RIP (Routing information protocol) - Automatically manages and exchanges routing information within a single autonomous system.
TCP (Transmission control protocol) - Reserves a constant connection between the two devices for the amount of time it takes for the data to be sent and received.
                                      Incorporates Error checking into its design. Used for situation such as file sharing, internet browsing or sending and email.
UDP (User datagram protocol) - Like TCP but less reliable and isn't as advanced. Any data sent via UDP is sent to the computer wheter it gets there or not.
                               Useful in situations where there are small pieces of data being sent. For example ARP and DHCP (Protocols for discovering devices.)








